 bool ChromeCrashReporterClient::GetCollectStatsConsent() {
+  // growser (#92): the registry value decides, in every build.
+  //
+  // This used to be a hard-coded true for non-official builds (#66). The reason
+  // was real: removing the telemetry (#38, #39) left the browser writing 0 into
+  // usagestats on every start, so crash uploads could never happen and the
+  // value could not even be set by hand. The cure was to stop reading it.
+  //
+  // Now the browser writes the user's own answer there instead - the checkbox
+  // on the welcome screen and the switch in settings, both bound to
+  // metrics::prefs::kMetricsReportingEnabled - so the value means something
+  // again and the constant can go. A person who says no is not asked twice by
+  // a build that ignores them.
+  //
+  // Policy still wins over both: SetUploadConsent() consults
+  // ReportingIsEnforcedByPolicy() before this value is used at all.
   return install_static::GetCollectStatsConsent();
 }
 
